Here is the commit message:
fixed a bug

Here is the root cause:
The GridView widget was being retrieved via `findViewById()`, but the code never explicitly called `setAdapter()` to bind the `imageAdapter` to it. This means the GridView had no data source attached, causing it to either display nothing, retain a stale/null adapter reference, or fail to reflect updates made to `imageAdapter`. Since `updateUI()` was called before the adapter was set on the GridView, any data population logic inside `updateUI()` (which likely modifies `imageAdapter`) would not be reflected in the UI because the view was never linked to that adapter instance in the first place. The missing `setAdapter()` call is the direct cause of the GridView failing to display or update items correctly.

Here is the patch:

     @Override
     public View onCreateView(LayoutInflater inflater, ViewGroup container,
                              Bundle savedInstanceState) {
         mainFragmentView = inflater.inflate(R.layout.fragment_main, container, false);
         mRequestQueue = Volley.newRequestQueue(getContext());

         // setup image adapter
         imageAdapter = new ImageAdapter(getContext());

         updateUI();
         gridview = (GridView) mainFragmentView.findViewById(R.id.gridView);
+        gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter);

         gridview.setOnItemClickListener(new AdapterView.OnItemClickListener() {
             @Override
             public void onItemClick(AdapterView<?> adapterView, View view, int position, long id) {
                 Intent intent = new Intent(getContext(), DetailActivity.class).putExtra(Intent.EXTRA_TEXT, position + "");
                 startActivity(intent);
             }
         });

         return mainFragmentView;
     }



